# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend environment
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values.
#
# Only VITE_-prefixed variables are exposed to the browser, and they are baked
# into the bundle at BUILD time, not read at runtime. Never put a secret here -
# anything in this file ships to every visitor.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Origin of the backend API. No trailing slash, and no /api suffix.
#
# LEAVE THIS EMPTY for the normal setup, where the API is same-origin:
#   - in development, Vite proxies /api to http://localhost:3000
#     (configured in vite.config.js)
#   - in production, Express serves the built SPA from the same host
#
# Only set it if you deploy the frontend and backend to separate origins, for
# example the frontend on Vercel and the API on Railway. It drives both the
# axios base URL and the Better Auth client, which must agree - otherwise the
# session cookie set at sign-in will not be sent with API requests.
#
# If you do split them, note two things:
#   1. The backend's FRONTEND_URL must be set to this app's own origin.
#   2. Two different registrable domains (vercel.app vs railway.app) are
#      cross-site, so the session cookie needs SameSite=None; Secure. That
#      requires extra Better Auth cookie configuration in backend/lib/auth.js
#      and is not set up by default.
#
#   Example: https://thinkpad-api.up.railway.app
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
